export anchor CandlelightStyle:
    number: 243
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Candlelight
    idea:
        A quiet near black page lit by warm candle glows, written as one
        narrow serif column like a letter, with the figures told in a
        sentence, projects as entries with a flame marking their progress and
        the fortnight drawn as a row of small candles.
    base: dark
    palette:
        night: #0c0907, the page and the style sheet
        glow: #271b10, the brightest point of any candle glow, the lightest surface text sits on
        hairline: #3a2a1c, rules, progress hairlines and the field underline at rest
        ink: #f0e2cc, text and figures
        muted: #bfa88a, meta, margin times, labels and axis text
        flame: #f2b366, the primary button, flames, this week candles, links and focus
        flameInk: #1e1206, text on flame
        wax: #8f7a63, last week candles
        ok: #b4d99a, On track text and check circle
        risk: #f2cf7a, At risk text and triangle
        bad: #f4a088, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
    type:
        One book serif stack, Charter, Bitstream Charter, Sitka Text, Cambria,
        Georgia, serif, for everything. Base 18px at 1.7. The greeting is 48px
        italic, section titles 26px italic, project names 21px, figures inside
        the summary sentence 30px italic with old style numbers, and margin
        times and meta 15px italic in muted. Labels are 13px small caps
        tracked 0.12em.
    layout:
        One 720px column centred on a near black page, with three soft candle
        glows behind it at the greeting, the projects and the chart. A quiet
        top line holds the italic Brightwork name, the six nav links as italic
        words split by middle dots with Home underlined in flame, a search
        field that is only a hairline underline, a bell, a flame New project
        pill and Mara Okafor. A small drawn candle with a glowing flame sits
        above the greeting Good morning, Mara, then the date in small caps and
        a coral line reading 4 tasks are overdue with a clock. The figures are
        written as a sentence, You have 6 active projects and 23 tasks due
        this week, 4 are overdue, and the team has logged 186 hours this week,
        with each number set large in italic. The projects are six entries
        split by hairlines, each the name with the status at right, then
        category, tasks and due date, and a hairline with a small flame at the
        percent and the percent beside it. The chart is a row of fourteen thin
        candles, wax for last week and flame topped for this week, height for
        the count and the count above, with the two week totals written
        beneath. Activity is a journal with italic times in a left margin.
        Below 640px the margin times move above each entry and the type steps
        down.
    spacing:
        An 8px unit. 32px between entries, 72px between sections, 24px column
        gutter on small screens.
    density: Sparse. One column, long line height and wide gaps.
    corners: Round pill buttons and round flames, otherwise no boxes at all.
    borders: Hairlines only, 1px at rest between entries and under the search field.
    shadows:
        No box shadows. Warmth comes from radial candle glows at 9 to 12
        percent and a soft blur round each flame.
    icons:
        Thin line icons at 1.5px stroke. Status uses a check circle, a
        triangle with a bang and a crossed square, always with the word,
        overdue a clock.
    focus: A 2px flame outline offset 4px with a soft flame glow.
    tone:
        Intimate and gentle, such as Good morning, Mara, A quiet note on the
        week and From the journal.
